\", \"reason\": \"SV-003: new-thread creation sets `title: deps.newThreadTitle ?? defaultThreadTitle(cwd)`; added exported `defaultThreadTitle(cwd)` (cwd leaf) + `newThreadTitle?` on ResolveDeps. Plus resolveThread modes (new/--session partial/--continue), parseLaunchFlags, registryArg/threadRefById.\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/picker.ts\", \"reason\": \"pickThread: cwd-scoped registry list (title + created) + injectable selection; empty cwd / cancel → null.\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\", \"reason\": \"SV-001: replaced placeholder `inferenceNotConfigured`/null-selector with real `defaultBuildSdkConfig` (observe-only SDK) and `defaultSelectThread` (most-recent --resume). SV-002: module-level `rememberedSessionThreadId` (survives connector teardown) + `resetSessionThreadMemory()`; reload reconstructs from it; onDispose keeps it only on reload, clears otherwise.\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/instance.test.ts\", \"reason\": \"TC-1.1 drives the PRODUCTION connector path (real default config + selector, only env overrides) asserting cwd + title + background instance; TC-1.4 flush+reattach.\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts\", \"reason\": \"Production-connector tests for TC-1.2 and TC-1.7 (--resume default selector); fresh-connector reload reconstruction + non-reload-clears (SV-002); no-flag-title (SV-003); parseLaunchFlags unit test; resolver/picker/restart coverage.\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/pi-lhc/test/smoke/extension-load.test.ts\", \"reason\": \"init/dispose block asserts real fail-closed behavior; hook-routing test redirected to a temp store so the now-real default does not write ~/.lhc.\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/pi-lhc/test/red-manifest.json\", \"reason\": \"Recorded for the two Story 1 lifecycle test files (verifier-directed updates).\" }\n  ],\n  \"tests\": {\n    \"added\": [\n      \"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/instance.test.ts: TC-1.1 (production path: cwd+title+background), TC-1.4 (flush+reattach) (2)\",\n      \"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts: TC-1.6 resolver modes, parseLaunchFlags, no-flag title, TC-1.7 picker, TC-1.5 restart, TC-1.2 connector, TC-1.7 connector --resume, TC-1.3 plain-data, TC-1.5 fresh-connector reload, non-reload-clears (10)\",\n      \"packages/lhc/test/threads-a8.test.ts: A-8 registry cwd/partial-id/ambiguous/cwd-filter/most-recent/migrate-on-read (11)\"\n    ],\n    \"modified\": [\n      \"packages/pi-lhc/test/smoke/extension-load.test.ts: init/dispose → real fail-closed behavior; hook-routing test redirected to a temp store\"\n    ],\n    \"removed\": [],\n    \"totalAfterStory\": 31,\n    \"deltaFromPriorBaseline\": 12\n  },\n  \"gatesRun\": [\n    { \"command\": \"pnpm --filter pi-lhc exec vitest run test/lifecycle/\", \"result\": \"pass\" },\n    { \"command\": \"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify\", \"result\": \"pass\" },\n    { \"command\": \"pnpm --filter pi-lhc green-verify\", \"result\": \"pass\" },\n    { \"command\": \"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify-all\", \"result\": \"pass\" },\n    { \"command\": \"pnpm --filter lhc verify\", \"result\": \"pass\" },\n    { \"command\": \"pnpm --filter lhc green-verify\", \"result\": \"fail\" }\n  ],\n  \"selfReview\": {\n    \"findingsFixed\": [\n      \"SV-001: production activate/session_start executes real lifecycle — `defaultBuildSdkConfig` constructs a real background SDK (no early fail-closed return) and `defaultSelectThread` resolves a real --resume selection; tests drive the connector with production defaults (only env overrides injected) for AC-1.1/1.2/1.7 (confirmed by named passing tests).\",\n      \"SV-002: reload reconstructs from durable state surviving teardown — the resolved id is module-level (not closure); the reload test creates a FRESH connector after teardown and proves reconstruction with a no-flag launch and no duplicate; the id is kept only across a reload and cleared on other teardowns (dedicated test).\",\n      \"SV-003: connector-created fresh threads carry title metadata (`defaultThreadTitle(cwd)`); TC-1.1 and the no-flag-title test assert cwd AND title.\",\n      \"Verified no ~/.lhc side effect: the smoke test's no-deps connector is redirected to a temp store now that the default is real.\"\n    ],\n    \"findingsSurfaced\": [\n      \"The Story-1 production provider is LHC's deterministic provider — an interim that makes the lifecycle real without a completing inference (blocked until @earendil-works/pi-ai is a build dependency). Never invoked in Story 1 (no capture → no derivation work); replaced by the PI-auth ModelCall in Story 5.\",\n      \"--resume production selection is most-recent-in-cwd because the local PI type surface exposes only `ui.notify` (no interactive prompt); an operator picker awaits a PI input surface.\",\n      \"Reload durable id is in-process module state: survives reload teardown, correctly dropped on process death (next launch re-resolves) — no sidecar/mapping, consistent with epic I-1.\",\n      \"Pre-existing lhc green-verify immutability drift on packages/lhc/test/retirement.test.ts (file byte-unchanged vs HEAD but mismatching the manifest hash from the Epic 05 closeout) is unrelated to this story; lhc verify (build/typecheck/lint/boundaries + 388 tests) passes.\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"openQuestions\": [\n    \"Is LHC's deterministic provider acceptable as the Story-1 interim production provider for observe-only Epic 1 (never invoked in Story 1; replaced by the PI-auth ModelCall in Story 5)? A real completing inference is blocked on @earendil-works/pi-ai not yet being a build dependency.\",\n    \"Confirm against the real PI dependency: the launch-flag spelling for the named-session mode (--session vs --session-id) and whether a PI input surface exists for an interactive --resume picker (the default currently resumes the most-recent cwd thread).\",\n    \"Title policy: connector-created threads use the cwd leaf as a provisional creation-time title (per the directive to add title metadata); TDQ Q4's richer derivation (e.g. first user prompt, Story 2+) remains deferred — confirm the cwd-leaf default is acceptable until then.\",\n    \"Pre-existing lhc immutability drift on packages/lhc/test/retirement.test.ts makes `pnpm --filter lhc green-verify` fail at the immutability step independent of this story; should it be re-baselined (out of this story's scope; not touched here)?\"\n  ],\n  \"specDeviations\": [\n    \"Production SDK provider for Story 1 is LHC's deterministic provider (interim), not the PI-auth-backed ModelCall (Story 5) — the completing-inference package (@earendil-works/pi-ai) is not yet a build dependency. The provider is never invoked in Story 1 because capture (Story 2) is not wired.\",\n    \"--resume production selection defaults to the most-recent cwd-scoped thread (no interactive input surface in the local PI types yet); the picker module remains fully cwd-scoped/titled and selection-injectable.\",\n    \"Reload reconstruction uses module-level in-process state for the durable resolved id (survives reload teardown; dropped on process death) rather than a PI-session→thread mapping or recovery sidecar (epic I-1).\",\n    \"resolveThread/pickThread take injected deps (cwd, registryPath, new-thread file path/title, selection) rather than the tech-design sketch's `(launch, pi: ExtensionAPI)` / `(cwd)` — ExtensionAPI carries none of those.\",\n    \"New thread title at creation = cwd leaf (`defaultThreadTitle`), a provisional Story-1 label; richer derivation is the deferred TDQ Q4.\",\n    \"A-8 added `ambiguous_thread_id` to lhc ErrorCode and a registry v2 migration (cwd) with migrate-on-read.\"\n  ],\n  \"recommendedNextStep\": \"Re-verify Story 1 (all blocking findings addressed; gates green). Then proceed to Story 2 (Event Capture and Turn Derivation) on the lifecycle seam. When @earendil-works/pi-ai and the PI extension packages become build dependencies, replace the deterministic interim provider with the PI-auth ModelCall (Story 5) and wire an interactive --resume picker; optionally re-baseline the unrelated lhc retirement.test.ts manifest entry.\"\n}","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"3bd99b80-3187-4d52-9c3e-b6b2c0cfc11e","total_cost_usd":1.542193,"usage":{"input_tokens":9,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12399,"cache_read_input_tokens":2374266,"output_tokens":9241,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12399,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5289,"cache_read_input_tokens":478425,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1893,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1893},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-8":{"inputTokens":9,"outputTokens":9241,"cacheReadInputTokens":2374266,"cacheCreationInputTokens":12399,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.542193,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"04650e4f-0175-4927-9c21-32befdbe4bca"}
